{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_logger", "label": "Logger interface", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Calls below the configured level emit nothing, but the arguments are still evaluated first because they are ordinary function arguments \u2014 guard expensive payloads with a manual level check."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_displayname", "label": "displayName()", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A path is an address, not a name, and under sharding it is unreadable. The name is added rather than substituted so source stays the path and nothing you correlate on moves; it is a label for humans, never an identity. Resolved per log call so it can read state and follow a restart \u2014 keep it cheap and side-effect free."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_setdisplayname", "label": "context.setDisplayName(name)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The way in for Behaviors actors, which all share one TypedActor class and have no subclass of yours to override."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_withdisplayname", "label": "ActorOptions.withDisplayName(name)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_jsonlogger", "label": "JsonLogger", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One newline-terminated JSON object per record for aggregation pipelines; Error instances serialise as name/message/stack because Error enumerable surface is empty, and circular refs, BigInt and functions are sanitised so a log call never throws. Writes to stdout by default \u2014 the right pipe for Docker, Kubernetes, vector, fluent-bit and jq."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_multi_sink", "label": "Multi-sink logging (withLogSinks)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_otellogger", "label": "otelLogger (OTLP logs bridge)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "@opentelemetry/api-logs is an optional peer dep the framework never imports \u2014 you bring your existing namespace import; the active span traceId/spanId link automatically when tracing runs in the same process."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_withfields", "label": "withFields (static structured fields)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bind it in preStart rather than a field initializer \u2014 this.context is not available until the actor is attached, so a field initializer would throw at construction."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_logcontext", "label": "LogContext (MDC)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Backed by AsyncLocalStorage so the context propagates across awaits, tells and cluster hops. Static withFields and dynamic MDC merge at emit time with dynamic winning on collision (innermost-scope-wins)."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_logcontext_run", "label": "LogContext.run / with / get", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "get() returns the live readonly context \u2014 the same reference for the whole scope, so never hold onto it past the scope or hand it to something that might mutate it."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_logcontext_runfresh", "label": "LogContext.runFresh", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The inverse of with(): where with inherits and adds, runFresh starts from empty. That fails safe \u2014 a field nobody set cannot leak \u2014 and is easier to reason about than remembering which keys to strip. Use it where work stops being attributable to the caller that started it."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_logcontext_runeach", "label": "LogContext.runEach", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Entries run sequentially, each in its own scope, ambient context ignored rather than merged. It returns Promise<void> because handing back results would read like Promise.all and invite use as a concurrency helper; an error propagates immediately and abandons the rest, since swallowing it would be a supervision decision inside a diagnostics primitive."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_logcontext_snapshot", "label": "LogContext.snapshot", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Returns a fresh copy on every call \u2014 the one to reach for at a boundary, safe to keep, mutate or serialise."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_logcontextentry", "label": "LogContextEntry<T>", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Exported so a queue that outlives the turn which filled it can be typed; capture the context at enqueue time, the only moment it is still current."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_mdc_propagation", "label": "MDC propagation across tell", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The runtime snapshots the current context onto the envelope and the receiver runs under a fresh run() of that snapshot; across nodes the snapshot rides on the wire envelope, so one correlationId stitches a multi-actor multi-node request together."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_context_per_envelope", "label": "Context is per envelope, not per async resource", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A delivery carries the context its tell snapshotted, or none \u2014 never whatever was ambient in the timer, socket callback or dispatcher tick that woke the actor. ReceiveTimeout, timer ticks, every Scheduler schedule, preStart/postStop and a context-free inbound frame all run with the MDC emptied, so a framework-delivered message never inherits the previous request."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_tenant_isolation", "label": "Deferred work and tenant isolation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "AsyncLocalStorage binds a store when the async resource is created, so a promise started inside a turn keeps that turn context forever and every tell its continuation makes stamps it onto the envelope. When the deferred work serves a different principal, one tenant identifiers travel with another tenant messages \u2014 a data leak, not just a confusing log line."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_mdc_json_safe", "label": "MDC values must be JSON-safe", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Values are string|number|boolean, enforced by the type, because across cluster hops the context serializes to JSON and arbitrary objects do not round-trip safely."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_typed_typed_actor_typedactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_setdisplayname", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_logger", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_displayname", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_displayname", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_setdisplayname", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_displayname", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_withdisplayname", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_logger", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_jsonlogger", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_logger", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_otellogger", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_logger", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_multi_sink", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_logger", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_withfields", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_withfields", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_logcontext", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_logcontext", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_logcontext_run", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_logcontext", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_logcontext_snapshot", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_logcontext", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_mdc_json_safe", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_logcontext", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_mdc_propagation", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_mdc_propagation", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_context_per_envelope", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_context_per_envelope", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_tenant_isolation", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_tenant_isolation", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_logcontext_runfresh", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_tenant_isolation", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_logcontext_runeach", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_logcontext_runeach", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_logcontextentry", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_logcontext_runeach", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_timers_and_scheduling_schedulererror", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_context_per_envelope", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_receive_timeout_no_diagnostic_context", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_context_per_envelope", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_timers_and_scheduling_tick_no_mdc", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_logcontext_runfresh", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_timers_and_scheduling_tick_no_mdc", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_jsonlogger", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_displayname", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": [{"id": "framework_delivered_messages_carry_no_mdc", "label": "Framework-delivered work runs with the MDC emptied", "nodes": ["docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_context_per_envelope", "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_receive_timeout_no_diagnostic_context", "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_timers_and_scheduling_tick_no_mdc", "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_logcontext_runfresh", "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_logcontext_runeach", "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_logging_tenant_isolation"], "relation": "form", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/logging.mdx"}]}